ESFMu: the doubled volume without shifting a negative number

ESFM_slot_generate_emu() doubles the output of a rhythm slot by shifting it
left by a flag. The output is a signed 13-bit sample, and the left shift of a
negative number is undefined behaviour whatever the shift, so
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the program as soon as an operator's output
goes below zero:

  src/chips/esfmu/esfm.c:1729:64: runtime error: left shift of negative value
  -23

A multiplication says the same thing and is defined. The flag is 0 or 1 and the
sample is 13 bits, so the product is far inside an int and int14 takes it as
before.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/esfmu/esfm.c b/src/chips/esfmu/esfm.c
index ce83a9d..5051622 100644
--- a/src/chips/esfmu/esfm.c
+++ b/src/chips/esfmu/esfm.c
@@ -1726,7 +1726,7 @@ ESFM_slot_generate_emu(esfm_slot *slot)
 
 	phase += *slot->in.mod_input & slot->in.emu_mod_enable;
 	slot->in.output = ESFM_envelope_wavegen(waveform, phase, slot->in.eg_output);
-	output_value = (slot->in.output & slot->in.emu_output_enable) << rhythm_slot_double_volume;
+	output_value = (slot->in.output & slot->in.emu_output_enable) * (1 << rhythm_slot_double_volume);
 	if (chip->emu_newmode)
 	{
 		slot->channel->output[0] += output_value & slot->channel->slots[0].out_enable[0];
